From ea3099aad8f49dcc8e937766f20fc9b92e20d063 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xob0t <32616886+xob0t@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:20:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 31/31] Virtual calls on this merged from several paths:
 through a merged entry address or nested merges

Patch 0008 recognizes a virtual call whose class pointer is merged from several paths. Two more shapes of the
same tail merging, seen on calls on "this", were left as "__call_indirect(__load8(m0), this, ...)": each way
computes the address of the same entry of the class ("class + 0x228") and the merged address is read for the
method and its description; or each way reads the method pointer itself and some ways are merges already (a
merge of merges), so the existing handling of merged method pointers saw no vtable entry. A merged entry
address is now the object's class plus the entry's offset, and a merge of merges whose every way picks one
virtual method on the call's receiver is that method. REWIND_NO_MERGED_VTABLE_ENTRIES and
REWIND_NO_NESTED_MERGED_TARGETS turn them off.
On a commercial Unity 6000.0.60f1 game 10 more Assembly-CSharp bodies are complete, none lost or changed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
